SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Temporary Changes to Referral and Authorizati
 on Processes Ending November 30\, 2026
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Temporary Changes to Referral and Authorization Process
 es Ending November 30\, 2026\nTemporary Changes to Referral and Authorizat
 ion Processes Ending November 30\, 2026\nOct 06\, 2026\nBeginning\nDecembe
 r 1\, 2026\n\, the Department will require members to complete a Single As
 sessment within the past 12 months before processing referrals\, prior aut
 horization requests\, and continued stay reviews for children’s medium- 
 and high-intensity services.\nAs\npreviously communicated\n\, the Departme
 nt temporarily reinstated direct-to-provider referral and prior authorizat
 ion processes while operational challenges with the Single Assessment proc
 ess were being addressed. That temporary process will end November 30\, 20
 26.\nThe Single Assessment process has stabilized significantly\, with ass
 essments now completed in an average of 7.5 business days after a request 
 is submitted.\nThank you for your continued partnership with the Single As
 sessment process.\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulle
 tins/temporary-changes-referral-and-authorization-processes-ending-novembe
 r-30-2026-2026-10-06
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/temporary-
 changes-referral-and-authorization-processes-ending-november-30-2026-2026-
 10-06
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
