UID:7ad6cd9fefd67b84@role-tax.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260916T165049Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Maine Logger’s Day - October 12
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, the logging industry has served as an economic dri
 ver and cultural tradition in Maine for centuries\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, the l
 ogging industry creates rural jobs and provides revenue for local communit
 ies\, contributing $534 million to the state’s economy annually\; and\nW
 HEREAS\n\, loggers provide renewable material for products used by people 
 in Maine every day\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, loggers are the root of Maine’s $8
 .3 billion forest economy\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, loggers are the means by whic
 h healthy and responsible forest management plans are accomplished\; and\n
 WHEREAS\n\, logging helps keep Maine’s forests healthy\, which support v
 ital animal habitats\, protect watersheds\, sequester carbon\, provide rec
 reational opportunities\, and limit wildfires\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, logging p
 rovides for healthy forests through regeneration to ensure the sustainabil
 ity of the industry for future generations of Maine people\;\nNOW THEREFOR
 E\n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of the State of Ma
 ine\, do hereby proclaim October 12\, 2026 as\nMaine Logger’s Day\nthrou
 ghout the State of Maine\, and I urge all citizens to recognize this obser
 vance.\nIn testimony whereof\, I have caused\nthe Great Seal of the State 
 to be\nhereunto affixed GIVEN under my\nhand at Augusta this tenth day\nof
  September Two Thousand Twenty-Six\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/of
 ficial_documents/proclamations/2026-09-maine-loggers-day-october-12
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-09-maine-loggers-day-october-12
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
