UID:ef8a13ba32d1558e@role-tax.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260908T210815Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Temporary Changes to Referral and Authorizati
 on Processes Ending November 30\, 2026
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Temporary Changes to Referral and Authorization Process
 es Ending November 30\, 2026\nTemporary Changes to Referral and Authorizat
 ion Processes Ending November 30\, 2026\nSep 08\, 2026\nBeginning\nDecembe
 r 1\, 2026\n\, the Department will require members to complete a Single A
 ssessment within the past 12 months before processing referrals\, prior
  authorization requests\, and continued stay reviews for children’s me
 dium- and high-intensity services.\nAs\npreviously communicated\n\, the De
 partment temporarily reinstated direct-to-provider referral and prior auth
 orization processes while operational challenges with the Single Assessm
 ent process were being addressed. That temporary process will end November
  30\, 2026.\nThe Single Assessment process has stabilized significantly\, 
 with assessments now completed in an average of 7.5 business days after a 
 request is submitted.\nThank you for your continued partnership with the 
 Single Assessment process.\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provi
 der-bulletins/temporary-changes-referral-and-authorization-processes-endin
 g-november-30-2026-2026-09-08
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/temporary-
 changes-referral-and-authorization-processes-ending-november-30-2026-2026-
 09-08
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5db6d661b605571c@role-tax.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260905T103232Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Management Track Assessment for American Plai
 ce and Gulf of Maine Haddock\; Public Meeting
DESCRIPTION:NMFS will convene the Management Track Assessment Peer Review 
 Meeting for the purpose of reviewing American plaice and Gulf of Maine had
 dock stocks. The Management Track Assessment Peer Review is a formal scien
 tific peer-review process for evaluating and presenting stock assessment r
 esults to managers for fish stocks in the offshore U.S. waters of the nort
 hwest Atlantic. Assessments are prepared by the lead stock assessment scie
 ntist and reviewed by an independent panel of stock assessment experts. Th
 e public is invited to attend the presentations and discussions between th
 e review panel and the scientists who have participated in the stock asses
 sment process.\nhttps://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/09/08/2026-
 18254/management-track-assessment-for-american-plaice-and-gulf-of-maine-ha
 ddock-public-meeting
URL:https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/09/08/2026-18254/manage
 ment-track-assessment-for-american-plaice-and-gulf-of-maine-haddock-public
 -meeting
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4b17db0d73e88aa6@role-tax.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260904T204459Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260904
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Looking Ahead: Eligibility-Dedicated Data Fee
 d to Support MaineCare Renewals and Enrollment
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Looking Ahead: Eligibility-Dedicated Data Feed to Suppo
 rt MaineCare Renewals and Enrollment\nLooking Ahead: Eligibility-Dedicated
  Data Feed to Support MaineCare Renewals and Enrollment\nSep 04\, 2026\nTw
 o weeks ago\, we\nannounced\ncommunications support for MaineCare partners
  and providers regarding changes the federal government is making to Maine
 Care (Maine’s Medicaid program) eligibility. This message provides an ea
 rly look at planned data-sharing that will help the Maine Department of He
 alth and Human Services (DHHS) verify information needed for MaineCare eli
 gibility. Our goal is to help eligible Mainers keep their coverage and acc
 ess to services with as little disruption as possible.\nNo action is neede
 d now.\nWe are sharing this information early to make providers aware of w
 hat is being planned. We will share more information as plans and timeline
 s are finalized.\nDHHS will continue to use administrative data sources it
  has access to as much as possible to support automatic (“passive”) re
 newals for MaineCare members. Federal changes to eligibility mean we need 
 additional information to help more eligible members maintain their MaineC
 are coverage. This data will help Mainers continue to benefit from MaineCa
 re\, which in turn will help providers minimize the impact of these federa
 l Medicaid cuts on their revenue and on their charity and uncompensated ca
 re.\nClinical Data Will Help People Stay Enrolled in MaineCare\nElectronic
  health record (EHR) systems contain clinical data that Maine and numerous
  other states are planning to use to help\nexempt\nMedicaid applicants and
  members with work-limiting health conditions from Work Requirements. In M
 aine\, this data will\nsupport MaineCare eligibility determination activit
 ies administered by the Office for Family Independence (OFI)\n. DHHS inten
 ds to partner with\nproviders to collect this information th\nhttps://www.
 maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/looking-ahead-eligibility-
 dedicated-data-feed-support-mainecare-renewals-and-enrollment
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/looking-ah
 ead-eligibility-dedicated-data-feed-support-mainecare-renewals-and-enrollm
 ent
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
